 Statement of Work
Contracting Organization: National Science Foundation (NSF), LIGO Scientific Collaboration
Contractor: Academic Parallel Computing Laboratory (ADVCS Program)
Project Title: Statistical Characterization of Transient Gravitational Wave Events
Contract ID: NSF-LIGO-EDU-24-B

1. Objective
The NSF seeks a software system to analyze gravitational wave strain data in order to characterize and categorize transient events, including both astrophysical signals and noise artifacts.
The goal is not detection alone, but population-level understanding of observed transients.

2. Scope of Work
The contractor shall:
Scan GW strain datasets for transient features
Compute simplified statistical descriptors for each candidate window
Map feature signatures into known transient categories
Aggregate results to reveal distribution trends
Identify and rank the most statistically significant events

3. Required Data Structures
The contractor shall implement and utilize:
A custom hash table for feature signature indexing
A tree-based structure to represent transient classification hierarchies
A heap-based priority queue for ranking significant transients
All teams shall use the same ADT interfaces to ensure comparability.

4. Deliverables
gw_results.csv – hierarchical transient classification
gw_topk.csv – highest-significance events
Parallel-safe, deterministic outputs

5. Success Criteria
Accurate aggregation of transient populations
Consistent classification across distributed runs
Clear, structured output suitable for downstream analysis


